type: software
title: "The Omega Centauri Society — Interactive Calculators for the NGC 5139 IMBH Question"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-14"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20689279"
url: "https://omegacentauri.me"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PostOakLabs/OCS"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Browser-based suite of interactive calculators for the Omega Centauri
  (NGC 5139) intermediate-mass black hole debate, Fermi Paradox analysis,
  and Macro Transcension Hypothesis. Covers stellar kinematics, pulsar
  acceleration constraints (TRAPUM 2026), Gaia DR4 forecasting, ADAF
  accretion SEDs, gravitational-wave horizon plotting, Bayesian evidence
  aggregation, and SETI exclusion limits. All tools are hash-addressable,
  reproducible, and MCP-exposed via mcp.omegacentauri.me. Curated data
  (measurements.js) is CC0; code is MIT; prose is CC BY 4.0.
